projects.description:
The overall objective and the project outcome are fully aligned with the thrust of Niue’s trade policy framework. Sustainable development opportunities ultimately depend on the country’s ability to access foreign markets. The project will provide Niue with a fully operational Electronic Advance Data (EAD) exchange interface between Customs and Post to support growing cross-border e-commerce flows, to strengthen and harmonise automated clearance processes, to apply advanced risk management techniques, and to adhere to international practices and procedures.

The implementation of an ASYCUDA-CDS interface in Niue will promote trade facilitation and e-commerce and reduce time and costs of trading across borders by:
i.	Increased efficiency and transparency in the clearance process for outbound and inbound items;
ii.	Increased accuracy and transparency in the calculation of duties and taxes;
iii.	Advance risk management techniques implemented to cope with increasing volume of postal consignments;
iv.	Integrated working arrangement implemented between Customs and Post operator;

Moreover, the ASYCUDA-CDS interface will also benefit the Government of Niue through:
i.	Improved information for Government decision-making; 
ii.	Improved management of border risk;
iii.	Support for the Government’s Trade Facilitation and e-commerce initiatives;
iv.	Support for MSME development with affordable and secure means of delivery of goods
